Description:

Two JMAP operations that could add message data to a user's mailboxes without
consulting the storage quota now enforce it.

Email/copy now charges copied messages against the destination account's
storage quota when the source and destination mailboxes are under different
quota roots.  Previously, an authenticated JMAP user could bypass quota
limits by copying mail from one account to another: the limits that applied
when writing new mail were not applied to cross-account copies.

EmailSubmission/set now charges the saved copy of an outgoing message against
the submitting user's storage quota.  For a futurerelease submission that
copy carries the full message body, so a user already at or over quota could
schedule large sends and grow their usage without limit.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-m78h-pxc5-h7wp.


